      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(4\\le X\\le 11)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we extend the endpoints of the interval $4\\le X\\le 11$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4\\le X\\le 11) & ≈P(4-0.5\\le Y\\le 11+0.5) \\\\  & =P(3.5\\le Y\\le 11.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
